{:edb/db-before-t 1137 :edb/db-after-t 1138 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534450 50 #inst "2026-10-07T04:54:27.904Z" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100521 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100521 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x}$." 13194139534450 false] [17592186100521 1145 "Let's set $u = \\ln x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\ln x}}dx &= 3∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= 3∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}du \\\\\n&= 3∫u^{-1/2}du \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2u^{1/2} + C \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{u} + C \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{\\ln x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 false] [17592186100521 1145 "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100522 1100 "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100522 1100 "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x}{x} \\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534450 false] [17592186100522 1145 "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2 }{x} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3({log}_{3}⁡x)^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100522 1145 "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2}{x} \\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x$. Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫((\\log_{3} x)^{2})/(x)dx &= ∫(\\log_{3} x)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫u^{2} \\cdot \\ln 3du \\\\\n&= \\ln 3∫u^{2}du \\\\\n&= \\ln 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}u^{3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln 3(\\log_{3} x)^{3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln 3\\log_{3}^{3} x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 false] [17592186100523 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}$." 13194139534450 false] [17592186100523 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}.$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100523 1145 "Let's set $u = \\ln x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x & e & e^{2} \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x &= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x} \\\\[5pt] &=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{7}{3} \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 false] [17592186100523 1145 "Let's set $u = \\ln x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n&= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n&=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2}\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right)\\[5pt]\n&=\\dfrac{7}{3}\t\t\n\n\t}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186100729 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288889 13194139534450 true] [17592186100729 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288896 13194139534450 true] [17592186100729 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288910 13194139534450 true] [17592186100729 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288931 13194139534450 true] [17592186100730 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288917 13194139534450 true] [17592186100730 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288924 13194139534450 true] [17592186100730 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288938 13194139534450 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288903 13194139534450 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288945 13194139534450 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288948 13194139534450 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288951 13194139534450 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288955 13194139534450 true] [17592186101057 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534450 true] [17592186101057 1100 "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186101057 1100 "Calculate the integral $∫(2)/(x\\ln (2x))dx$." 13194139534450 false] [17592186101057 1145 "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186101287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534450 true] [17592186101287 1100 "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186101287 1100 "What is $∫\\frac{\\log_{2} x}{x}dx$?" 13194139534450 false] [17592186101287 1145 "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186101290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534450 true] [17592186101290 1100 "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186101290 1100 "What is $∫(\\log_{3} (x^{2}))/(x)dx$?" 13194139534450 false] [17592186101290 1145 "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}).$Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\int u\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{log}_{3}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186288889 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288890 13194139534450 true] [17592186288889 1089 "q-13803" 13194139534450 true] [17592186288889 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534450 true] [17592186288889 1100 "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186288889 1113 #uuid "a2a8959c-6b04-5ef7-8052-da57da0ea3d3" 13194139534450 true] [17592186288889 1145 "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{u}^{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534450 true] [17592186288890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288891 13194139534450 true] [17592186288890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288892 13194139534450 true] [17592186288890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288893 13194139534450 true] [17592186288890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288894 13194139534450 true] [17592186288890